	(text "ETHERNET: LAN8720A 10/100 RMII PHY (replaces the IP101GRI: KiCad symbol, ESP-IDF lan87xx driver, cheap\nbreakouts for Phase 1). 25 MHz crystal; REFCLKO (pin 14) feeds the P4 REF_CLK in (GPIO50) through 33R.\nStraps: REGOFF=0 (int. 1V2 on), nINTSEL=0 (REFCLKO, 10k pull-down), PHYAD0=1 (address 1), MODE=111 (10k\npull-ups: the P4 pins load the straps). LEDs active high via 270R. DS00002165: REFCLKO-mode timing is outside\nthe RMII spec - verify with the P4 in Phase 1 (fallback: 50 MHz oscillator into XTAL1, nINTSEL=1).\n3V3_ETH is switched (EXP_EN_ETH): firmware keeps the RMII/MDIO/reset pins low or hi-Z while it is off.\nTXD1 = GPIO35 = P4 BOOT strap: the PHY TXD1 input has no pull, the 4.7k pull-up on the MCU sheet wins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 233.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
